 "reading": "The initializer runs std::env::args() over the whole argv in order, argv[0] included, with no early exit: the constructor collects the C argv cells into a vector from index 0, and next() converts each element through the UTF-8 validator, unwrapping at library/std/src/env.rs:864:51. Each argument of length >= 2 starting with \"--\" is skipped. Every other argument contributes one lowercased piece to an accumulator via format!(\"{} {}\", acc, piece): the piece is the argument itself, except that an argument containing \"/cham/\" contributes its last path component truncated at its last \"-\"; such an argument ending in \"/\" fires the build_mode.rs:28:13 assertion instead. After the last argument the accumulator is lowercased again and stored. The stored value therefore starts with a space whenever anything contributed and is never exactly \"debug\", \"release\" or \"run-client\"; \"run-client\" contributes only \"run\" through the /cham/ path. The static and getter carry no source name in the artifact (no BUILD_MODE / BuildMode / build-mode string exists); the naming evidence is the module path base/src/build_mode.rs and the assertion local name \"arg\"."
